cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Detection limits for lunar water ice in Chandrayaan-2 DFSAR
  compact-polarimetric data: analysis code and verification gates
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  accompanying paper. The satellite data is not part of this
  software and carries separate terms; see DATA.md.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Saksham
    family-names: Raina
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # PLACEHOLDER - author to replace
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Sakshamraina07/LunarIceIntelligence'
abstract: >-
  Code, derived artifacts and verification gates for a study of the
  detection limits of a CPR-based lunar water-ice criterion applied
  to a single Chandrayaan-2 DFSAR L-band pass over the lunar south
  pole. Contains no Chandrayaan-2 or LOLA data; every figure and
  number is regenerated from products obtained separately from
  PRADAN and the NASA PDS.
keywords:
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - compact polarimetry
  - equivalent number of looks
  - detection statistics
  - lunar water ice
  - Moon
  - planetary radar
  - speckle
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-13'
